phase P1
title Static foundation

tasks
    T001
        title      Reconcile the public Implementation route contract
        status     done
        priority   medium
        description
            Historical contract deliverable: reconcile the root Implementation runtime value
            with its same-name public type, and assign route and provider ownership. The
            runtime namespace has exactly succeed, effect, and merge. Provider construction
            remains owned by T006; route assembly remains owned by T007.

            Source phase Epic: flow-state-e7p.1 (closed in the retained Beads record), with
            direct children flow-state-e7p.1.1 through flow-state-e7p.1.12 (all closed).
            Child IDs and receipts are recorded in their owning Workflow Tasks below; Beads
            statuses are historical provenance, not current Workflow readiness.

            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.1.9 (closed). Its route-choice decision, Bead
            flow-state-e7p.1.2, records the user's selection and is absorbed here rather
            than tracked as implementation work.

            Historical write scope: reference/incident-console/implementation/contracts/
            PUBLIC_API.md and IMPLEMENTATION_WORKFLOW.md. Evidence: Bead closure receipt.
        acceptance
            Historical closure receipt: the then-active contract pack named the root runtime
            Implementation value and its same-name public type, with exactly succeed, effect,
            and merge. It assigned one production owner to the route and another to provider
            construction; it added no alias, alternate route, or Object.freeze requirement.
            This records the historical contract decision, not current semantic authority.

            Historical contract review found no blocking conflict. Focused typecheck and
            diff check passed at closure. The broad lint failure was recorded as an existing
            baseline. These are historical receipts, not current-checkout results.
        derives_from [@plan.PublicSurface.D1, @plan.Verification.D3, @plan.Verification.V1]

    T002
        title      Implement definition and event inference
        status     done
        priority   medium
        description
            Historical production deliverable: implement callback-or-null definitions,
            nominal events, exact literal inference, and input, memory, and context types.
            Validate authored structure synchronously with one private Schema; retain the
            memory initializer without running it during construction.

            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.1.3 (closed). Allowed write scope:
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/definition/**, including its local test/.
            Evidence: definition tests, package typecheck, lint, and Bead closure receipt.
        acceptance
            Compile proofs retain exact definition ID, state, event, payload, context,
            operation, input, and memory types without casts, wrappers, or explicit generics.
            Runtime proofs accept depth ten and reject depth eleven, invalid names, duplicate
            or malformed states, invalid declaration kinds, excess fields, and malformed
            event payloads. Construction runs no memory initializer, event factory, selector,
            actor, or operation.

            Hostile reflection, sparse arrays, custom container prototypes, and mutation
            during construction are outside the rejection contract. The focused definition
            test, package typecheck, lint, workspace check, and diff check passed historically.
            Do not read that receipt as a current-checkout result.
        derives_from [@plan.Types.D1, @plan.Types.C2, @plan.Types.V1, @plan.Verification.D6]

    T003
        title      Prove the definition-to-machine composition seam
        status     done
        priority   medium
        parent     [@task.Rewrite.T004]
        description
            Historical child deliverable: prove that machine construction consumes the
            already-built nominal Definition value, preserves its identity, and infers exact
            state and event tokens through the callback. Keep this seam synchronous and inert;
            the full grammar belongs to T004.

            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.1.4.1 (closed), child of flow-state-e7p.1.4.
            Allowed write scope: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/machine/ and its local test/.
            Evidence: focused machine proof and Bead closure receipt.
        acceptance
            The production-owner proof retains Definition identity and exact state, event,
            and event-argument types; rejects structural impostors and foreign tokens; and
            executes no initializer, factory, Schema decode, Effect, actor, or work.
            Machine production code does not revalidate the authored Definition.

            Historical format, lint, package typecheck, focused machine test, and diff check
            passed. The parent machine task remained open at this child receipt. No current
            checkout check is implied.
        derives_from [@plan.Types.D1, @plan.Types.V1, @plan.RuntimeV2.V1, @plan.Verification.D3]

    T004
        title      Implement recursive machine grammar and pure compiled tables
        status     done
        priority   medium
        blocked_by [@task.Rewrite.T002]
        description
            Historical production deliverable: compile the exact recursive machine grammar
            and inert lookup tables in packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/machine/, with local
            tests. Consume the constructed Definition without decoding or validating it again.
            Runtime activities, timers, and onMemory ordering belong to later owners.

            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.1.4 (closed). Expected definition/machine failures
            were migrated separately by T009; preserve that ownership boundary.
        acceptance
            Compilation rejects malformed or ambiguous grammar before runtime work and
            proves exact recursive states, events, defaults, targets, reentry, handlers, and
            tokens. Ordinary terminal-looking leaves remain legal. Unsupported child,
            final, history, parallel, entry/exit, invoke, always, Boolean-reentry, and
            timer-owned finite-action forms remain rejected.

            Machine compilation performs no Schema decode, duplicate Definition validation,
            callback execution, or actor/runtime work. Focused typecheck, machine tests,
            lint, format, and diff check passed historically; this does not assert they pass
            on the current checkout.
        derives_from [@plan.Types.D1, @plan.Types.V1, @plan.PublicSurface.V2, @plan.Verification.D3]

    T005
        title      Implement canonical operation and family types
        status     done
        priority   medium
        blocked_by [@task.Rewrite.T002]
        description
            Historical production deliverable: define resource, transaction, and stream
            descriptors; exact P/K/A/E/R propagation; closed family states; and inert finite
            actions in one cohesive operation feature with local tests. Runtime Cause
            classification belongs to a later owner.

            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.1.5 (closed). Allowed write scope:
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/operation/**. Evidence: type proofs, operation
            tests, lint, and Bead closure receipt.
        acceptance
            Compile proofs retain exact P/K/A/E/R and family unions, including transaction
            options, stream latest-value and terminal fields, and typed outcome unions.
            They reject widened parameters, invalid family shapes, parent-captured types,
            generic registries, and stream actor cancellation. They do not claim runtime
            Cause classification or operation behavior.

            Package typecheck, lint, focused operation tests, format, and diff check passed
            historically. No current-checkout result is implied.
        derives_from [@plan.Types.V2, @plan.Types.C2, @plan.PublicSurface.V3, @plan.Verification.V1]

    T006
        title      Implement closed App.M, requirements, and inert Implementations
        status     done
        priority   medium
        blocked_by [@task.Rewrite.T001, @task.Rewrite.T002, @task.Rewrite.T004, @task.Rewrite.T005]
        description
            Historical production deliverable: compile exact module and App.M records,
            AppPlan identity, normalized acyclic requirement carriers, descriptor and machine
            admission, and immutable typed Implementation providers. Construction remains
            inert; Runtime acquisition, Scope, finalization, and ready() belong to Phase 2.

            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.1.6 (closed). Provider constructors live in one
            feature-owned module with local tests; route re-exports belong to T007. The
            historical static harness belongs to T008, not this Task.
        acceptance
            Pure construction acquires nothing and rejects duplicate or unclosed identity,
            cycles, foreign or unadmitted machines/descriptors, and post-construction
            extension. Requirements remain exact without recursive carrier blowup, dynamic
            roots, or registries. succeed, effect, and merge preserve exact provider types,
            remain inert, and reject duplicate service identity. No namespace Object.freeze
            behavior is required.

            Historical typecheck, lint, 23 focused tests, and independent contract/Effect
            reviews passed. Runtime acquisition and lifecycle remain deferred. These receipts
            describe the accepted snapshot only.
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Types.D2,
                     @plan.Types.D3,
                     @plan.Types.V3,
                     @plan.PublicSurface.V4,
                     @plan.Verification.D3,
                     @plan.Verification.V1
                     ]

    T007
        title      Implement package routes, public errors, and remediation
        status     done
        priority   medium
        blocked_by [@task.Rewrite.T001, @task.Rewrite.T006]
        description
            Historical production deliverable: assemble exact isolated package routes,
            facade-only public exports, immutable structured usage errors, and the stable
            code, documentation, and remediation mapping. Keep raw Cause only on the two
            permitted public errors; human wording remains actionable but is not a
            compatibility surface.

            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.1.1 (closed). Route files are package.json,
            src/index.ts, src/public/root.ts, and src/public/types.ts; error implementation
            and local tests stay in a cohesive feature module. The route-choice decision in
            flow-state-e7p.1.2 is represented by T001. The lint disposition from decision
            flow-state-e7p.1.10 is historical context, not a separate implementation Task.
        acceptance
            Packed consumers prove exact isolated names, route identity, and deep-import
            rejection; immutable structured error fields; and all 18 stable code,
            documentation, and remediation rows. Representative tests prove messages are
            non-empty and actionable. The root Implementation runtime value has exactly
            succeed, effect, and merge alongside its same-name type, with no alias, alternate
            or private route, or duplicate provider authority.

            The maintained quickstart compiles from source and packed declarations; its actor
            turn receipt remains later-phase work. Route tests and the historical packed,
            type, lint, and final Phase 1 receipts passed on their recorded snapshots only.
        derives_from [
                     @plan.PublicSurface.D1,
                     @plan.PublicSurface.V1,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsV2.V3,
                     @plan.Verification.D3
                     ]

    T008
        title      Build the correctness-only static proof harness
        status     done
        priority   medium
        blocked_by [@task.Rewrite.T004, @task.Rewrite.T005, @task.Rewrite.T006, @task.Rewrite.T007]
        description
            Historical proof deliverable: add positive and negative compile fixtures for
            accepted names and inference, invalid static shapes, declarations, and inert
            pure compilation. Cover strict and isolated declarations, packed consumers,
            React 18/19, and representative small and medium consumers.

            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.1.7 (closed). The user-authorized correctness-only
            disposition controls: compiler-performance budgets, benchmark arithmetic,
            performance baselines, and reports are not acceptance gates. Do not restore
            superseded measurement work. Allowed write scope: one cohesive declaration-proof
            feature under packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/<feature>/ with local test/;
            packed-consumer fixtures and package scripts remain integration boundaries.
        acceptance
            Valid consumers preserve exact inference and requirements; invalid shapes fail;
            declarations contain no any or assertion erasure; and pure compilation proves
            inertness and closed-world identity. Pinned-compiler fixtures cover the accepted
            public type families and packed surface. Compiler errors, including excessive
            instantiation, remain failures; no performance threshold is required.

            Historical focused type, packed, lint, and static-harness checks passed. The
            final Phase 1 review reused recorded evidence and added packed checks. This is
            a historical receipt, not a claim about the current checkout.
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Types.V1,
                     @plan.Types.V2,
                     @plan.Types.V3,
                     @plan.Types.V8,
                     @plan.Types.V9,
                     @plan.Types.V10,
                     @plan.Verification.V1
                     ]

    T009
        title      Migrate definition and machine failures to Diagnostic
        status     done
        priority   medium
        blocked_by [@task.Rewrite.T002, @task.Rewrite.T004]
        description
            Historical failure-boundary deliverable: use Result and the shared Diagnostic
            for expected definition and machine validation failures. Keep structural Schema
            failures, semantic failures, and impossible invariant defects distinct; preserve
            exact paths and details without re-decoding or executing Effects.

            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.1.11 (closed). Allowed write scope is the definition
            and machine production owners and their local tests. Runtime, Story, CLI,
            public route implementation, frozen package, and contract-authoring work are
            outside this Task.
        acceptance
            No expected invalid-authoring path escapes as a generic Error. Machine reasons
            are exhaustive; paths and details are stable; impossible validated-state
            violations remain defects. Production proofs distinguish Schema, Result, and
            defect lanes, and prove malformed definitions/configurations and no acquisition.

            Historical package typecheck, definition and machine tests (15 focused tests),
            lint, format, diff check, and independent reviews passed. These receipts are not
            current-checkout results.
        derives_from [
                     @plan.DiagnosticsV2.D2,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsV2.V2,
                     @plan.Verification.C2,
                     @plan.Verification.V1
                     ]

    T010
        title      Prepare partial static evidence for closed owners
        status     done
        priority   medium
        blocked_by [@task.Rewrite.T004, @task.Rewrite.T005, @task.Rewrite.T006]
        description
            Historical partial evidence deliverable for the already-closed definition,
            machine, operation, App, and Implementation surfaces. Cover medium and recursive
            carrier controls, invalid-shape fixtures, declaration emit, and the currently
            available negative compile cases.

            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.1.12 (closed). This is preparation only: it does not
            close T008 or the final packed, root-route, or quickstart lanes. Its user-
            authorized correctness-only instruction supersedes references to a performance
            baseline or regression ceiling; do not reinstate either gate.
        acceptance
            The TypeScript 7.0.2 fixtures preserve exact RequirementsOf and reject recursive
            carrier and invalid static shapes. Emitted declarations contain no any or
            assertion erasure. Checks for the available owners passed historically, with
            the remaining packed, root, and quickstart lanes named as blocked; the full
            harness remained owned by T008.

            Historical receipts do not establish current results or complete T008.
        derives_from [@plan.Types.V3, @plan.Types.V8, @plan.Types.V9, @plan.Verification.V1]

